        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Coral reefs cover ~284,000 km² — about 0.1% of ocean floor — yet host an estimated\n25% of all marine species. That is the Connell Paradox: enormous biodiversity in\nnutrient-poor tropical water. The mechanism is not input richness; it is tight internal\nrecycling and the intermediate disturbance regime."
    },
