        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Coral Reef Ecosystems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ENERGY FLOW:\n  Zooxanthellae fix CO₂ → glucose → 90%+ of coral energy needs\n  Coral polyp provides: CO₂, NH₄⁺, shelter, light orientation\n  Herbivorous fish (parrotfish, surgeonfish) → keep algae off coral\n  Predatory fish → top-down control of herbivores\n  Tight nutrient cycling: dead organisms → bacteria → nutrients\n    reabsorbed by algae → eaten by animals → back to coral\n  Net nutrient import from ocean: minimal\n```"
    },
