        "title": "Coral Reef Ecosystems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Tentacles (nematocysts for prey capture)\n            │    │    │\n     ───────┤    │    ├─────────  Oral disc\n            └────┼────┘\n                 │   Mouth\n                 │\n                 │   Coelenteron (gastrovascular cavity)\n                 │   lined with gastrodermis containing\n                 │   ZOOXANTHELLAE (Symbiodinium)\n                 │\n       ┌─────────┴─────────┐\n       │   Calicoblast     │\n       │   epithelium      │\n       └─────────┬─────────┘\n       (Secretes CaCO3 skeleton below: calcium carbonate deposition)\n                 │\n    ┌────────────┴───────────────┐\n    │  CALCIUM CARBONATE         │\n    │  SKELETON (corallite)      │\n    │  CaCO₃ aragonite           │\n    │  Accumulated over decades  │\n    │  to centuries              │\n    └────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
