      "text": "WHY CORALS ARE COLORED:\n  Coral tissue is nearly transparent\n  ZOOXANTHELLAE contain chlorophyll a and c (brown/yellow)\n  + coral fluorescent proteins (green/red/blue — photoprotection)\n  Combined appearance: brown/tan/yellow (zooxanthellae) +\n                       vivid colors (fluorescent proteins)\n```"
