        "root_concepts": "[coral, reefs]",
        "section": "marine-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Coral Reef Ecosystems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  HEAT STRESS                                        │\n  │       │                                             │\n  │       ▼                                             │\n  │  Photosystem II dysfunction in zooxanthellae        │\n  │  (PSII is temperature-sensitive)                    │\n  │       │                                             │\n  │       ▼                                             │\n  │  Excess excitation energy → reactive oxygen         │\n  │  species (ROS) production                           │\n  │  (O₂⁻, H₂O₂, ·OH)                                   │\n  │       │                                             │\n  │       ▼                                             │\n  │  ROS damages both zooxanthellae and coral tissue    │\n  │       │                                             │\n  │       ▼                                             │\n  │  CORAL EXPELS ZOOXANTHELLAE                         │\n  │  (adaptive response? or damage response?            │\n  │   still debated — probably both)                    │\n  │       │                                             │\n  │       ▼                                             │\n  │  WHITE SKELETON visible through transparent tissue  │\n  │  Coral: ALIVE but starving                          │\n  │       │                                             │\n  │   ┌───┴────────────────────────────┐                │\n  │   │ Stress < 4 weeks               │ Stress prolonged│\n  │   ▼                                ▼                │\n  │  RECOVERY                      MORTALITY            │\n  │  (zooxanthellae recolonize)    (weeks-months)       │\n  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
